+# Staff invitation flow inspection
+
+Selected task: `001 Inspect iteration 028's Staff invitation model, commands, acceptance journey, routes, emails, and profile-completion flow.`
+
+## Iteration 028 checkpoint context
+
+Iteration 028 was merged in commit `cefa3ee` (`iteration 028: Staff member invitations with profile completion`). That commit added the Staff invitation flow, shared invitation feature scenarios, web/controller tests, domain/API tests, acceptance step plumbing, and the `membership_club_invitations` projection table.
+
+The iteration 028 task list is fully checked off in `docs/iterations/028-staff-member-invitations/todo.md`, so the current implementation should be treated as the foundation for Membership Admin invitations rather than duplicated.
+
+## Staff invitation domain model
+
+The Staff invitation lifecycle lives inside the Membership bounded context:
+
+- Aggregate: `Memba.Membership.ClubInvitation`
+- Commands:
+  - `Memba.Membership.Commands.InviteClubMember`
+  - `Memba.Membership.Commands.ResendClubMemberInvitation`
+  - `Memba.Membership.Commands.AcceptClubMemberInvitation`
+- Events:
+  - `Memba.Membership.Events.ClubMemberInvited`
+  - `Memba.Membership.Events.ClubMemberInvitationResent`
+  - `Memba.Membership.Events.ClubMemberInvitationAccepted`
+- Projection schema/projector:
+  - `Memba.Membership.Projections.ClubInvitation`
+  - `Memba.Membership.Projectors.ClubInvitation`
+- Router: `Memba.Membership.Router` routes the invitation commands to `ClubInvitation`.
+
+The projection table is created by `web/priv/repo/migrations/20260608032753_create_membership_club_invitations_projection.exs` with:
+
+- `invitation_id` primary key.
+- `club_id`, `email`, `normalized_email`, `token_hash`, `status`.
+- accepted person/membership IDs.
+- `resend_count`.
+- unique `token_hash`.
+- partial unique index on `{club_id, normalized_email}` for pending invitations only.
+
+Important lifecycle rules in `ClubInvitation`:
+
+- A new invitation validates caller-supplied invitation and club IDs, normalizes email, and stores only a token hash.
+- A second invite against the same aggregate is rejected while pending or accepted.
+- Resend only works for a pending invitation and rotates the token hash.
+- Accept only works for a pending invitation and records accepted person and membership IDs.
+
+## Public Membership API to reuse
+
+`Memba.Membership` already exposes the core invitation lifecycle:
+
+- `invite_club_member/2`
+  - generates an invitation ID if the caller did not supply one;
+  - generates a plaintext one-use token and stores only `InvitationToken.hash_token/1`;
+  - rejects an email that already belongs to an active club member with `{:error, :already_active_member}`;
+  - detects an existing pending invitation for the same club/email and resends it instead of creating another pending row;
+  - returns `{:ok, %{invitation_id: ..., invitation_token: ...}}`.
+- `resend_club_member_invitation/2`
+  - finds a pending invitation by ID or `{club_id, email}`;
+  - rotates the token and returns the fresh plaintext token.
+- `accept_club_member_invitation_for_existing_person/2`
+  - accepts only a pending invitation;
+  - requires the existing person to have the invited email address;
+  - creates an ordinary active membership;
+  - marks the invitation accepted.
+- `complete_invited_club_member_profile/2`
+  - accepts only a pending invitation;
+  - rejects blank/invalid names through the person creation command path;
+  - creates the person with the invited email;
+  - creates an ordinary active membership;
+  - marks the invitation accepted.
+- Query helpers:
+  - `get_club_member_invitation/1`
+  - `get_pending_club_member_invitation_by_email/2`
+  - `get_club_member_invitation_by_token/1`
+  - `active_member_of_club_by_email?/2`
+
+The existing API has no inviter/actor attribute. Staff callers use it directly from the Staff-only route. Iteration 029 should either add an authorized club-member entry point around this shared lifecycle or add a clear actor distinction without giving Staff implicit club membership.
+
+## Token rules
+
+`Memba.Membership.InvitationToken` is separate from ordinary auth sign-in tokens:
+
+- plaintext tokens are 32-byte URL-safe random strings;
+- Membership persists only SHA-256 hashes encoded as lowercase hex;
+- invitation tokens do not expire in this slice;
+- pending unknown-invitee links are not consumed on first open;
+- accepted invitation tokens remain findable so re-opening an accepted link is idempotent and does not create duplicate membership.
+
+This matches the iteration 028 inspection note in `docs/iterations/028-staff-member-invitations/auth-token-onboarding-inspection.md`: invitation links grant membership and must not be mixed with ordinary short-lived auth tokens.
+
+## Staff route and UI surface
+
+Routes in `MembaWeb.Router`:
+
+- Staff invitation form:
+  - `GET /admin/clubs/:club_id/invitations/new`
+  - LiveView: `MembaWeb.Admin.ClubMemberInvitationsLive.New`
+  - inside the `/admin` scope and `:staff_browser` pipeline.
+- Invitation callback/profile completion:
+  - `GET /invitations/club-members/:token`
+  - `GET /invitations/club-members/profile`
+  - `POST /invitations/club-members/profile`
+  - Controller: `MembaWeb.ClubMemberInvitationController`
+
+The Staff form is email-only:
+
+- selector `#club-member-invitation-form`;
+- input `#club-member-invitation-email-input`;
+- submit button `#send-club-member-invitation-button`;
+- no invitee name field.
+
+`MembaWeb.Admin.ClubsLive.Show` exposes the Staff entry point from the Staff club detail member list:
+
+- `#invite-member-link` links to `/admin/clubs/:club_id/invitations/new`;
+- direct add-member submission now redirects to the invitation page with an informational flash;
+- existing person edit links remain available.
+
+## Email delivery
+
+`Memba.Membership.ClubMemberInvitationEmail.deliver/1` owns invitation email composition and Swoosh handoff.
+
+Required attrs:
+
+- invitee email;
+- club context with non-blank name;
+- one-use invitation URL.
+
+Behaviour:
+
+- normalizes recipient email;
+- uses auth email sender configuration (`Memba.Accounts.AuthEmail`);
+- sends through `Memba.Mailer`;
+- subject is `You're invited to join <club name>`;
+- text/html bodies include `/invitations/club-members/:token`;
+- text explicitly says the link can be used once to create membership;
+- no expiry language;
+- supports provider metadata for Postmark message stream and Resend tags.
+
+Staff LiveView currently builds the URL as:
+
+```elixir
+MembaWeb.Endpoint.url() <>
+  "/invitations/club-members/" <> URI.encode(invitation_token, &URI.char_unreserved?/1)
+```
+
+Iteration 029 can reuse this email module, but a shared URL helper may be useful if both Staff and Membership Admin UI surfaces need to send invitation emails.
+
+## Acceptance and profile-completion journey
+
+`MembaWeb.ClubMemberInvitationController.callback/2` handles invitation links:
+
+1. Look up the invitation by plaintext token hash.
+2. Missing/invalid tokens redirect to `/auth` with an invalid-link flash and no sign-in.
+3. Pending invitation for an existing complete person:
+   - calls `Membership.accept_club_member_invitation_for_existing_person/2`;
+   - signs the browser in as the invited email;
+   - clears invitation session state;
+   - redirects to the invited club URL.
+4. Pending invitation for an unknown email:
+   - signs the browser in as the invited email;
+   - stores `club_member_invitation` session state with invitation ID, club ID, and email;
+   - redirects to `/invitations/club-members/profile`;
+   - leaves the invitation pending and token reusable.
+5. Accepted invitation:
+   - signs in as the invited email;
+   - clears invitation session state;
+   - redirects to the invited club URL without creating another membership.
+
+`profile/2` and `complete_profile/2` require the verified invitation journey session and matching current identity email. Unknown invitees submit only their name in `profile.html.heex`. A blank name leaves the invitation pending. A valid name calls `Membership.complete_invited_club_member_profile/2`, creates the person, creates ordinary active membership, accepts the invitation, signs in, and redirects to the club.
+
