+
+Web tests covering Staff UI and callbacks:
+
+- `web/test/memba_web/live/admin/club_member_invitations_live/new_test.exs`
+- `web/test/memba_web/controllers/club_member_invitation_controller_test.exs`
+- related auth preservation tests in `web/test/memba_web/controllers/auth_controller_test.exs`.
+
+Shared acceptance feature:
+
+- `acceptance-tests/features/club_member_invitations.feature`
+  - Staff scenarios are implemented and un-todoed under `@iteration-028`.
+  - Membership Admin scenarios are already present under `@iteration-029 @todo-domain @todo-ui`.
+
+Step plumbing:
+
+- `web/test/features/step_definitions/club_member_invitation_steps.exs` exercises the domain/application layer directly.
+- `acceptance-tests/features/step_definitions/club_member_invitation_steps.js` and `acceptance-tests/features/support/club_member_invitations.js` exercise the Staff UI through Playwright.
+
+Current acceptance helpers assume invitation actors go through the Staff route/sign-in path. Iteration 029 will need to extend, not duplicate, that plumbing so Membership Admin actors use the new member-facing route and ordinary members get a clear rejection.
+
+## Implications for iteration 029
+
+- Reuse `Membership.invite_club_member/2`, `ClubMemberInvitationEmail.deliver/1`, and the existing callback/profile-completion controller wherever possible.
+- Add authorization before the invitation is created/sent for club-member actors with `club.manage_members`.
+- Keep Staff route behaviour intact; it is already Staff-pipeline protected and tested.
+- Membership Admin accepted invitations already create ordinary memberships only because acceptance uses `AddMember` and never assigns roles.
+- Duplicate active member rejection and duplicate pending resend are already shared lifecycle rules; Membership Admin tests should prove they are reached through the authorized member-facing entry point.
+- A future implementation should be careful not to consume an unknown invitee's token on first callback open.
+
+## ADR conformance evidence
+
+- ADR 0002 / 0007: invitation lifecycle is in the Membership Commanded context with commands, aggregate, events, router, and public application service.
+- ADR 0009: invitation read model uses Commanded Ecto projections.
+- ADR 0010: acceptance scenarios remain in the shared `acceptance-tests/features/club_member_invitations.feature` file with Elixir and JS step plumbing.
+- ADR 0011: invitation, person, and membership IDs are caller/application generated UUID-like IDs; aggregates do not generate identities.
+- ADR 0013: Staff web flow is covered with PhoenixTest/Phoenix LiveView/controller tests from user-visible behaviour.
+- ADR 0016: invitation emails use the existing Swoosh/Mailer boundary and auth email provider configuration rather than direct provider HTTP calls.
+- ADR 0022: existing flows use strong consistency for browser-facing command dispatch; later Membership Admin routes should keep read-your-writes behaviour explicit when navigating/rendering from projections.
